<%# Cerberus override of Blacklight::Response::ViewTypeButtonComponent's
    template, for `turbo: false` — the toggle swaps a whole results column and
    the frame-less full load is what keeps the sidebar controls in step.

    The caption is hidden rather than dropped: the buttons read as icons, and
    the text is what names them for a screen reader. Blacklight marks it hidden
    in the markup rather than from a stylesheet, so the class belongs here. %>
<%= link_to url, title: label, aria: aria_attributes, data: { turbo: false }, class: "#{Array(@classes).join(' ')} view-type-#{ @key.to_s.parameterize } #{"active" if selected?}" do %>
  <%= icon %>
  <span class="caption visually-hidden"><%= label %></span>
<% end %>
